From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: negotiate DSC rates, MST streams and PCON color conversion

Preserve per-commit/per-stream DSC ownership, exact chunk bytes, OEM DTO phase
padding and independent PPS banks. Keep link FEC separate from shared decoder
and passthrough AUX references. Admit optional source 420 and advertised PCON
RGB-to-YCbCr conversions with a checked AUX transaction and precise TMDS budget.

OEM contracts: MiCode display 44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
msm/dp/dp_panel.c, dp_catalog.c and msm/sde/sde_encoder_phys_vid.c,
Copyright (c) 2012-2023 The Linux Foundation and Qualcomm Innovation Center.
MST AUX/reference and PCON protocol comparison: signed Linux 7.3,
drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c and drm_dp_mst_topology.c.
Retain existing file-level GPL-2.0-only notices. No foreign board values.

The AVR arithmetic supports a 32-bit pixel period; O82 receiver admission keeps
its separate lower-floor guard. This is not a physical 1 Hz support declaration.

